  "id": "Compound::DB00549 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Zafirlukast exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c8 and Cyp2c19, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of these enzymes in the epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities of arachidonic acid, which ultimately result in the activation of Cyp2e1. The evidence suggests that Zafirlukast may influence Cyp2e1 through the modulation of arachidonic acid metabolism, potentially by enhancing or inhibiting its enzymatic activity. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible relationship, with the shared pathway involving arachidonic acid metabolism as a critical mediator. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Cyp2e1 underscores the potential role of Zafirlukast in modulating Cyp2e1 activity through the arachidonic acid metabolic cascade.",
